  "question": {
    "text": "A body A of mass <math><mi>m</mi></math> is moving in a circular orbit of radius <math><mi>R</mi></math> about a planet. Another body B of mass <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> collides with A with a velocity which is half <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> the instantaneous velocity <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> of A. The collision is completely inelastic. Then, the combined body:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
